# D-WHOLE-PAGE-CAW-PAYLOAD-PANICS-NODE-IN-SCSI-ALLOC-SGTABLES: the fix at its
# natural rate, after tests/queues/caw_span_adjacent_ab.queue (lapq_spanadj1,
# 2026-10-19 05:13-05:18Z) graded CONFIRMED AND FIXED: both control arms
# panicked at scsi_alloc_sgtables+0x3a1 (R15=2, RAX=0x2000), both fix arms
# answered 837 and 875 adjacent-page whole-page commands as two bvecs each.
#
# This queue removes the test knob: the fix build (this tree,
# 65863B924040AF5213F2A76) at its defaults (caw_span=1, payload pages from
# alloc_page, adjacent only by the allocator's chance) on the same rig and
# shape as the panics (2/net/mesh/direct g2c, test29 first node).  Natural
# rate before the fix: 4 of 5 g2c preps of the first build carrying the
# whole-page swap panicked their first node in mount(2) (and 1 of 2 on g2e).
# Each lap: a default prep (both nodes mount with caw_span=1), then three
# natural-page rounds on test29 (tests/caw_span_adjacent_ab.sh with adjacent
# 0: umount, mount, 100 creates, sync; caw_span_n read every round).
#
# PREDICTION: every prep completes (rc 0) and every arm PASSes (caw_span_n
# rising every round, no panic, boot id unchanged), 10 of 10.
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap): FIXED AT ITS NATURAL RATE if all
# 10 preps and all 10 arms pass with no BUG, Oops or panic on either node's
# serial console; FIX FAILS on any panic, attributed from its own lines first.
# A prep that fails for another reason is read from its own lines; an arm that
# is VACUOUS (no whole-page command answered) measured nothing.
#
# Bounds: prep 300 (as the A/B queue), an arm 305 (its header, ROUNDS=3).
#
# Run spannat1 (tests/evidence/lapq_spannat1.log, 05:19-05:29Z) completed the
# laps commented out below, 9 preps and arms natd1..natd8, every one rc 0 and
# every arm PASS; the session relay ended the runner during natd9 (lap 18),
# which left no verdict.  The laps still uncommented are the rest, run as
# spannat2 with a prep first so natd9 starts from a restored fleet.
